---
/**
 * Privacy Policy. Describes what the website actually does (verified in the
 * code: no forms, no accounts, no analytics, no cookies, no third-party
 * scripts, fonts/media self-hosted) and the Google AdSense disclosures Google
 * requires. The advertising wording follows src/data/ads.ts automatically.
 * Approved by BIA (November 2026): operator "Boma's Intellectual Academy",
 * official email in src/data/site.ts.
 */
import DocPage from '../components/DocPage.astro';
import { adsEnabled } from '../data/ads';
import { cbt, email, office, primaryContact, site } from '../data/site';

const updated = '2026-11-13';
---

<DocPage
  title="Privacy Policy | BIA JUPEB — Boma’s Intellectual Academy"
  description="How BIA JUPEB (Boma’s Intellectual Academy) handles personal information on biajupeb.com.ng and when you contact us, including advertising cookies and Google AdSense."
  eyebrow="Privacy"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  lead="How we handle personal information when you use this website or contact BIA JUPEB, and the choices you have."
  updated={updated}
>
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    This website, <strong>biajupeb.com.ng</strong>, is run by {site.parent} (“BIA”, “we”, “us”), which offers the BIA JUPEB
    programme. BIA is the data controller for the personal information described in this policy. You can reach us at
    {' '}<a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> or using the other details in <a href="#contact">Contact us</a> below.
  </p>
  <p>
    This policy covers this website and enquiries made to BIA. BIA’s CBT practice platform at {cbt.host} is a separate website and
    is not covered by this policy.
  </p>

  <h2>Information collected when you use this website</h2>
  <p>
    This website has no sign-up, no account, no contact form and does not take payments. You can read every page without giving
    us any personal information.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical information.</strong> Like every website, our hosting provider (Vercel) receives the information your
      browser sends when it requests a page — such as your IP address, browser type, the page requested and the time. It is used
      to deliver the website and keep it secure.
    </li>
    {adsEnabled ? (
      <li>
        <strong>Cookies.</strong> BIA does not set cookies or use analytics on this website. Our advertising partner, Google, uses
        cookies to show ads — see <a href="#advertising">Advertising</a> and our <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>.
      </li>
    ) : (
      <li>
        <strong>Cookies.</strong> This website does not currently set any cookies and does not use analytics or tracking tools.
        See our <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>.
      </li>
    )}
  </ul>

  <h2>Information you give us directly</h2>
  <p>
    When you call, send a WhatsApp message or visit our offices, we receive the details you choose to share — usually your name,
    phone number and your questions about the programme. If you register, the admissions office also asks for the documents
    listed on this website: your O’Level result (or awaiting result), National Identification Number (NIN) and birth
    certificate.
  </p>
  <p>
    We use this information to answer your enquiry, to process your registration and to keep in touch with you about your
    studies. We keep it only as long as we need it for these purposes or to meet legal obligations, and we do not sell it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Messages sent through WhatsApp, Facebook or TikTok are also handled by those services under their own privacy policies.
  </p>

  <h2>Students and staff shown on this website</h2>
  <p>
    Students are named or pictured on the Hall of Excellence and success stories pages only where BIA has confirmed their
    permission; other results are shown without names. Staff names, photographs and phone numbers are published with BIA’s
    approval. If you appear on this website and want something changed or removed, contact us and we will act on your request.
  </p>

  <h2 id="advertising">Advertising</h2>
  {adsEnabled ? (
    <p>
      This website shows advertisements served by Google AdSense. Ads are labelled “Advertisement” and are kept separate from
      BIA’s own content. BIA does not choose individual ads and does not endorse the products or services advertised.
    </p>
  ) : (
    <p>
      This website does not currently show advertisements. We intend to show ads served by Google AdSense in future. When we do,
      the following will apply, and ads will be labelled “Advertisement” and kept separate from BIA’s own content.
    </p>
  )}
  <ul>
    <li>
      Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user’s prior visits to this website or other
      websites.
    </li>
    <li>
      Google’s use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to users based on their visit to this website
      and/or other sites on the Internet.
    </li>
    <li>
      You may opt out of personalised advertising by visiting Google’s
      {' '}<a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Ads Settings</a>. You can also opt out of
      some third-party vendors’ use of cookies for personalised advertising at
      {' '}<a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">www.aboutads.info</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Google explains how it uses information from websites that show its ads at
      {' '}<a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener" target="_blank">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Visitors in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland will be asked for consent before advertising
      cookies are used, through a consent message provided by Google.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>
    This website links to other services, including WhatsApp, Facebook, TikTok, Google Maps and BIA’s CBT practice platform.
    Their own privacy policies apply when you use them.
  </p>

  <h2>Where information is processed</h2>
  <p>
    Our hosting provider{adsEnabled ? ' and Google' : ''} may process technical information on servers outside Nigeria. Where
    this happens, we rely on those providers’ safeguards for international transfers.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023 you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>ask what personal information we hold about you and get a copy;</li>
    <li>ask us to correct information that is wrong or incomplete;</li>
    <li>ask us to delete your information, or to restrict how we use it;</li>
    <li>object to how we use your information, and withdraw any consent you have given.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To use any of these rights, contact us as shown below. If you are not satisfied with our response, you can complain to the
    {' '}<a href="https://ndpc.gov.ng" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Nigeria Data Protection Commission</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Children and young people</h2>
  <p>
    This website is for prospective JUPEB students, parents and guardians. It is not directed at children under 13. If you are
    under 18, please involve a parent or guardian when you contact us or register.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We will update this page if our practices change — for example when advertising starts — and change the “Last updated” date
    above.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    For privacy questions or requests, email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> with “Privacy” in the subject line, or
    contact BIA at:
  </p>
  <address>
    <strong>{site.parent}</strong><br />
    {office.name}<br />
    {office.lines.map((l) => <>{l}<br /></>)}
    Phone / WhatsApp: <a href={`tel:${primaryContact.phone}`}>{primaryContact.display}</a>
  </address>
</DocPage>
